# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# Written explicitly because gcloud's default is `#!include:.gitignore`, and
# this repository's .gitignore excludes `data/processed/*` -- which silently
# dropped `tables.duckdb` from the upload. The build still succeeded and the
# deployed Data Analysis agent would have had no tables to query.
#
# .dockerignore still filters what reaches the image; this only bounds the
# upload. Anything the image needs must survive BOTH.

.git
.gitignore
.gcloudignore

# Secrets. .env.cloud holds live credentials and must never be uploaded.
.env
.env.cloud

# Not part of the backend image.
frontend/
docs/
eval/
data/scripts/

# Build and test artefacts.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
backend/.venv/
backend/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# Runtime state. `data/raw` and `data/processed/tables.duckdb` are deliberately
# NOT excluded: the image bakes them in because a cloud host has no volume.
data/qdrant/
data/uploads/
**/.~lock.*#

.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
